# Environment variables
#
# Static QR creation is browser-only and needs no backend or secrets. Dynamic
# QR is an optional hosted feature; see README.md for the Worker secrets and
# deployment instructions.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (or `.env.local`) and fill in real values.
# Never commit `.env` — it is git-ignored via `*.local`; add `.env` to
# .gitignore explicitly if you rename it.

# Vite exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to client code — anything here is
# PUBLIC. Never put a real secret in a VITE_ variable.

# The public URL of the deployed site, e.g. https://qr.example.com
# Used at build time for canonical links, Open Graph URLs, sitemap.xml and
# robots.txt. Without it the build skips the static per-page HTML and the
# sitemap (and warns) rather than pointing at a wrong domain.
# VITE_SITE_URL=

# Optional hosted dynamic QR API. This is opt-in and separate from local QR
# generation. Its public URLs store destinations on the configured service.
# VITE_DYNAMIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com

# Where the "Support this project" link in the footer points to. The first
# one that is set wins: Ko-fi, then Buy Me a Coffee, then GitHub Sponsors.
# Without any of them the link points to the GitHub Sponsors page of the
# repository owner.
# VITE_KOFI_URL=
# VITE_BUY_ME_A_COFFEE_URL=
# VITE_GITHUB_SPONSORS_URL=
